{
  "slug": "karellen-rr-mcp",
  "name": "Karellen Rr Mcp",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Claude Code plugin for rr reverse debugging via MCP. Automatically configures the karellen-rr-mcp MCP server and includes a crash detection hook that suggests rr when a command exits with a signal (SIGSEGV, SIGABRT, etc.) or sanitizer output is detected, a debugging skill with the full record-replay-analyze workflow, and an rr-investigator agent for autonomous crash investigation through reverse execution. Requires Linux x86-64 with rr, gdb, and pip install karellen-rr-mcp.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**, **1 agent**, **3 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `rr-debug` (Debug a crash or test failure using rr reverse debugging), `rr-debug-logic` (Debug a logic bug (wrong output, wrong value, incorrect behavior) using rr), `rr-debug-race` (Debug a data race or concurrency bug using rr), `rr-debug-test` (Debug a failing test using rr)\n- **Agents** (1): `rr-investigator` (Use this agent when a command or test exits with a signal (SIGSEGV, SIGABRT, SIGBUS, SIGFPE), produces a…)\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`, `PostToolUseFailure`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `karellen-rr-mcp`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install karellen-rr-mcp@claude-community` from `karellen/karellen-rr-mcp`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 3,
    "mcp": 1
  },
